            <ArticleTitle>Dilutional acidosis complicating rotational atherectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>627-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rotational atherectomy is an important technique for the relief of atherosclerotic disease in both coronary and peripheral arteries. Here, we describe an unusual complication, dilutional metabolic acidosis, due to hydration during rotational atherectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
